diff --git a/domains/findings/pages/the-catalog-cli-is-alive-behind-two-akasha-commands-that-refuse.finding.ts b/domains/findings/pages/the-catalog-cli-is-alive-behind-two-akasha-commands-that-refuse.finding.ts
index b51c4d40f090f340065529ea29ec47ac820391ce..56516b0e26bda619eb1f2e2b48c3159e14f9467f 100644
--- a/domains/findings/pages/the-catalog-cli-is-alive-behind-two-akasha-commands-that-refuse.finding.ts
+++ b/domains/findings/pages/the-catalog-cli-is-alive-behind-two-akasha-commands-that-refuse.finding.ts
@@ -8,5 +8,5 @@ export const theCatalogCliIsAliveBehindTwoAkashaCommandsThatRefuse = {
   claim:
     "A survey called `temper/catalog-cli` the closest call to an unreached package in temper. It is reached: two live command entry points read it through one adapter, and the two akasha commands meant to replace them both answer a refusal naming the very code it holds. Its `src/index.ts` is `export {}`, which is what made it read as unreached. The two modules that carry the work have landed as `temper-catalog-side-file`.",
   evidence:
-    "`temper/catalog-cli/src/index.ts` is one line, `export {}`. A reader taking the package's root export as the package finds nothing there. The manifest names two more ways in, and both are read.\n\n`tools/lib/temper-catalog-code.ts:3` takes `resolveSavedVariablesPath` and `resolveSideFilePath` from `@temper/catalog-cli/temper/catalog/paths`, and `:7` takes `computeNextSideFile`, `parseSideFile`, `SideFile` and `serializeSideFile` from `@temper/catalog-cli/temper/catalog/side-file`. That adapter is read by `tools/commands/temper/catalog/invalidate.ts` at lines 55, 77, 80 and 81, and by `tools/commands/temper/catalog/status.ts` at lines 97, 98 and 108. Both are commands a person runs today.\n\nThe akasha side names the same work and cannot do it. `akasha/temper/temper-commands/temper-catalog-invalidate/temper-catalog-invalidate.command.code.ts` answers `refused` with `the catalog addon's registry of domains is not in akasha yet, so nothing here writes a request`, and `temper-catalog-status.command.code.ts` answers `the catalog addon's capture reader is not in akasha yet, so nothing here reads its state`. The command pages beside them state the whole behaviour, down to the version the addon weighs against the last version it saw.\n\nSo the package is neither unreached nor already landed. `akasha/temper/temper-catalog-core/apply-invalidations` holds the addon-side half, which reads a request and drops the domains named; nothing in akasha wrote a request or resolved either path before this.\n\nThe lesson for the census. An `export {}` root plus a manifest whose other ways in are read only from `tools/` reads as unreached to anything counting importers of the package name alone. Count the ways in the manifest names, one at a time.",
